WEBVTT

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:03.260
Welcome home.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.360
I baked some cookies, so eat them, okay?

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.200
It looks like your father is going to be staying at the lab again tonight.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.450
I'm going to be late, too, so go ahead and eat dinner without me.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.870
It's in the refrigerator...

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:21.360
The Cosmic Fracture is still surrounded by many mysteries.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.700
It is predicted that...

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.440
...after the emergency supreme council meeting...

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.130
...which is slated for Sunday, there will be some kind of announcement.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:29.840
All right!

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.540
Hello!

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:11.730
Episode Twenty: 
Let There Be a Future For You

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.370
When you finish eating that, I'll take you home.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.030
It's all right, it's all right. I'm going to stay over.

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:15.820
Again? Isn't your mother worried?

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.970
If she were worried, she'd come home earlier.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.780
Her work must be tough. I'm sure of it.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:23.510
I know.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.620
Both of them care about their work more than they care about me.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:29.250
Why are you saying such kiddy things?

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:33.950
But I am a little kid. They're always working.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.780
It's just for a bit more. Just be patient.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.400
But I'm tired of being patient.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:42.130
Coming!

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.690
Thank you for always feeding her.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.380
Oh, no...

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.880
Our ice cream is the cheap stuff, so it's all right...

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:50.690
Arisa!

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.030
Come again!

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:53.610
Okay!

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:01.790
Hey. 
Hmm?

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.340
How about we have a party this Sunday?

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.480
You can call all of your friends...

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:07.580
Really?

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:11.600
Yes. It looks like your father will have a break from his work, too.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:16.170
I'm so happy! Let's have it!

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:38.610
Atomic disassembly... just from being touched by the Fracture?

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.340
According to the simulation...

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.540
What a horrible thing.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.050
This Sunday?

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.970
Yeah! Shipon and Arisa said OK!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.880
It's all right with me.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:50.920
Me, too.

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:52.440
What about Pierre and the others?

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:53.530
I haven't asked them yet.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.900
Then leave that to me!

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.810
Okay! Thanks!

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:01.740
Are they under an order of silence or something?

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.030
Even though they were that open during the Second Wave?

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:06.560
I know.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:09.260
Things feel a little different this time.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.050
The Cosmic Fracture...

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.650
It's pretty troublesome, isn't it?

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:16.370
So all we can do is wait for the supreme council meeting, I guess.

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:17.090
Um...

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:21.430
A party?

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:24.780
It's in gratitude for what happened on the Ultima.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:28.830
We didn't really do anything worth being thanked for, though...

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:31.780
Okay, I understand. We'll be there.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:33.340
You're okay with that, right?

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.270
Acknowledged. 
Yes. Yes.

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:36.540
Well, there you have it.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:38.140
Okay, I'll tell them.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.540
It looks like Miss Katase has regained her footing.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:50.930
So it would seem...

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:56.360
Yes... thank goodness...

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:57.800
Yeah.

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:18.830
So there are no mistakes in the calculations?

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:19.410
No, sir.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.560
So the first ones to make contact with it will be us on Pluto...

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:33.380
The Cosmic Fracture seems like a Calabi Yau space that has opened up.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:37.340
I'd like those theories to be put into practice in some other solar system...

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:41.110
Yeah, no kidding... So what do you want to do for lunch?

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.610
I'm eating fast food today.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.470
Don't push yourself too hard. See you!

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:48.120
Right!

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:56.060
Can I sit with you?

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:56.760
Hmm?

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:02.210
What?

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:04.780
You have to give up your lunch break?

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:07.530
Monitoring the DLS must be tough.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:09.980
Well, it's not that bad...

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:11.980
You can make it to the party, right?

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.660
Yeah, well...

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:16.060
In that case, that means everyone's going to be attending!

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:19.010
And now the question is who we'll be escorting.

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:20.220
Want to go with me?

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:25.050
Yes, yes, you're going with Akira, right?

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.260
Well, yeah.

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:28.560
This upsets me in a nonsexual way.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:31.900
Miss Ayaka and the others said okay!

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:34.620
All right! That's everyone!

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:35.860
Everyone?

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:38.760
Yeah, everyone's going to come. Kouta said he's coming, too!

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:40.660
I see...

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:51.050
We have two months left.

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:53.240
This is the greatest crisis in our history.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:55.780
It looks like the governor of the Akapusu...

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:57.380
...is going to be attending the meeting as well.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:59.230
Professor Turner, huh?

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:02.120
Even if he was a prominent figure during the Great Mission...

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.060
...he's old news now.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.140
This is our era.

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:09.200
Another way to put it is that this crisis is our perfect chance.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:11.370
That way of thinking is so like you.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:27.130
Professor Turner?

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:36.300
Well, I never expected you to come alone.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.990
I've never been any good with such grandiose things, after all.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:43.440
I don't think there is a role for an old fool like myself, though.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:48.580
Orihara, it appears you're going to be the chairman of this meeting.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.270
Show me your skills!

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:50.870
Yes, sir.

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:56.570
This Sunday?

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.120
Yeah, that's right.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:00.350
There shouldn't be any problems at the meeting.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.260
I might be able to make it in time for tea...

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:04.610
It's all right if you come in the middle, too!

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:06.780
It counts as long as you're there!

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:08.050
Hey, now.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.560
What kind of present should we bring?

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:19.230
A drink after finishing your shower really is the best!

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.320
It's not the best.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:24.740
Yes, yes. Well, showing up empty-handed is not so great...

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:28.750
I wonder if something like a housewarming gift would be all right?

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.420
A housewarming gift? Like what?

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:34.570
Like hand towels?

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.630
Be sure to actually talk to Kouta.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:38.180
What?

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:40.840
Okay...

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:44.460
Good work.

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:46.450
Thanks.

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:50.100
Is the meeting really going to be all right?

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.190
Yeah.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.880
The summary about the Fracture has already...

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:55.990
...been distributed in written reports...

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:59.900
...so that each of the Foundations can prepare themselves.

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:22.770
I'm looking forward to Sunday...

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:30.060
It certainly is a magnificent view.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:30.980
Yes.

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:36.070
The Second Wave can't even be compared to the current crisis.

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:39.830
It is the greatest one in the history of all humanity...

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.400
Don't make a big deal out of it...

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.900
We will now begin the emergency supreme council meeting.

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:50.910
Technical Officer Kazamatsuri, if you would.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.420
Kazamatsuri

00:10:13.780 --> 00:10:14.940
Hello!

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:16.700
Hi!

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:17.630
Come in!

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:20.860
This place is nice and quiet.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:24.220
They said there wasn't enough space in the residential section.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.490
It feels like we were lucky to have the Ultima get blown away.

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:29.190
That's pretty radical of you all of the sudden.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:31.650
It's all right. Today, everyone can speak their mind.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:33.100
And you really are.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:36.050
All present, stand in line!

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:38.240
Bow to the Big Four!

00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:39.820
Hello!

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:40.990
Hello.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:42.120
That was very taigi.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:46.110
What do you mean by "taigi"?

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:51.000
It used to be a term for a national ceremony, but...

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:52.850
...in other words...

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:55.300
...it means "well done."

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:56.430
Oh, I see.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.840
Hey, Kouta! What are you doing just standing there?

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:03.260
Here, come over here!

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:04.560
Right.

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:06.670
According to our theories on the great himo...

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:10.720
...we think there may actually be six more dimensions separate...

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.720
...from the four that we are able to confirm.

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.780
They are rolled up in Calabi Yau spaces...

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:20.550
...that are ten to the negative thirty-fifth power in meters...

00:11:20.750 --> 00:11:21.790
...and are closed off.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:26.330
So those are the dimensions inside those Calabi Yau spaces, right?

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:27.290
Yes.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:31.590
There is probably no mistake in viewing the Cosmic Fracture...

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:32.750
...as being those six dimensions opened up.

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:34.830
A tear in space-time, is it?

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:36.600
It's three billion kilometers long?

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:38.170
A super dimensional space... I can't imagine it...

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:45.340
Both this and that, it's all too delicious.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:49.230
My mother made all of it. Do you want to take some back with you?

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:49.920
Yeah!

00:11:53.050 --> 00:11:55.130
I wish he'd come home soon...

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:58.170
Those two were certainly surprising.

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:00.110
That's... true.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.450
You're doing all right, too, being with Miss Katase.

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:04.270
And it's a party today, too.

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:10.000
Shipon. 
Hmm?

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:14.240
Kouta seems kind of sad. We're all right here, so...

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:15.110
Later, later!

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:18.700
We need to cook this quickly. I'm sure that everyone's starving.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:24.710
Thank you very much for what you did at the Ultima.

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:27.580
Oh, no. We didn't do anything important.

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:30.440
Is Technical Officer Kazamatsuri at the supreme council meeting?

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:31.220
Yes...

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:33.100
Speaking of that...

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:35.760
The Cosmic Fracture, right?

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:39.490
The Cosmic Fracture itself possesses gravitational fields...

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:43.230
...and when it passes by bodies of high mass...

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:44.260
...like the sun and the planets...

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:47.080
...it is certain to change their orbits...

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:48.980
...in order to make contact with them.

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:52.940
In other words, it's certain to come to the Sol System.

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:55.550
What will the effect be when it makes contact?

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:58.080
The surface boundary of the material that is touched...

00:12:58.260 --> 00:13:02.280
...will be collapsed on the atomic level and destroyed.

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:05.300
What will happen when it makes contact with a fixed star?

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:06.990
There are no exceptions.

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.540
Due to the collapse on the atomic level...

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:11.650
...the nuclear fusion reaction of the fixed star...

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:13.870
...will become more violent and cause a supernova explosion.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:16.820
In other words, the cause of Hydrus Beta's explosion...

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:19.210
...was the Fracture making contact with it...

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:23.700
...and it can be possibly be said that both the First and Second Waves...

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:26.080
...were nothing but the forerunners.

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:29.430
This time, the Sol System will be destroyed...

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:36.920
In a situation like this, isn't the boy supposed to talk to the girl first?

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:40.010
I'm thinking of talking to her. But...

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:43.540
...making a girl cry is pretty bad, isn't it?

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:45.740
It wasn't your fault, right?

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.210
What should I do?
Who knows?

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:49.870
What?

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:53.170
I'm not good with these kinds of things, either...

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.480
...even though I'm acting that way right now.

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:57.100
Really?

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:00.860
I kept thinking that I would be able to get advice from you.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:03.680
I'm sorry I'm not of any help.

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:08.790
But talking to you has made things a little easier, sempai.

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:10.200
Really?
Yes.

00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:11.590
Thank goodness.

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:19.340
The greatest problem is our time restraint.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:20.150
Right.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:22.100
When will the data be analyzed...

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:24.520
...and when will the basic countermeasures be considered?

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:25.960
I'd like for us to cooperate...

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.710
...and make progress in deciding on an evacuation plan.

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:31.340
Because if we calculate from current orbits...

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:34.780
...the first planet it will contact will be ours, Pluto.

00:14:35.130 --> 00:14:36.620
We're already past the two-month waiting period...

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:38.170
...until it arrives at the Sol System.

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:42.180
If we don't begin considering defense plans soon, we won't make it in time.

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:44.820
If we don't allay the fears of the citizenry...

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.010
...we won't be able to utilize our intelligence properly.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:49.120
How the evacuation should be executed...

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:50.220
...is an essential point to discuss.

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:52.680
If we have at least a week, then we can complete an evacuation.

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:57.680
Please refrain from making disorderly comments.

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:01.850
The Sol System will be destroyed...

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:04.580
My bad feeling is on the mark...

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:07.630
This time there isn't a 189-year postponement.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:10.020
Just two months...

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:12.840
Even still, I'm sure we can overcome this...

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:14.590
...just like we have up until now.

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:18.300
No matter the time, no matter what it is, there is always a possibility.

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:23.330
What about the Great Wall?

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:25.700
A barrier made up of gravitational fields...

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:28.270
...will simply pull in the Fracture, won't it?

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:29.410
As you say...

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:33.600
...the Great Wall is powerless against the Cosmic Fracture.

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:38.770
Using physical power is not a mistake.

00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:42.650
After all, its speed was reduced by the explosion...

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:44.620
...caused by the gravitational collapse of the Ultima.

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:48.320
Indeed. It is by no means an adversary we cannot deal with.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:51.320
What would you say...

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:53.720
...to creating a black hole, like in the case of the Ultima?

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:58.320
No, one that is on a much larger scale.

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:00.640
We tried calculating that.

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:03.240
It seems impossible.

00:16:03.980 --> 00:16:04.390
Yes.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:12.720
I wonder if Father isn't going to make it...

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:14.540
Yes, I wonder...

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:21.400
It really looks delicious.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:25.590
Yeah. It was all handmade by Miss Natasha.

00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:37.130
Then I propose we establish working groups and discuss particular cases.

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:38.050
I have no objections.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:41.150
Are you all right with being so slow?

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:43.110
This is a race against time.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:45.230
Are you saying we should just abandon Pluto?

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:46.380
I understand how you feel...

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:50.780
...but shouldn't we be thinking about the entire Sol System here?

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:53.210
I'm not saying this because of my ego!

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:55.290
I was just stating the facts.

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:56.990
I would like to withdraw!

00:16:57.540 --> 00:16:59.540
Silence! Please be silent.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:03.300
The first thing we need to consider is how to fight this thing!

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:06.640
That's right! Evacuation is meaningless!

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:07.350
That's right!

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:09.730
That's too extreme! It's unreasonable!

00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:12.550
There is no other way to survive except to defend the Sol System.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:14.710
We have to be absolutely certain on every point.

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:19.660
All we have to do is reverse calculate how to best use the two months!

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:21.010
That's right, that's right!

00:17:21.090 --> 00:17:22.730
There's only two months left!

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:25.880
Both laying the groundwork for things and heckling, huh?

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.170
They certainly are easygoing.

00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:30.860
It's your turn next, Rinna.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.110
If you lose, then you have to play a penalty game.

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:35.160
That's right, a date with me.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.200
What?

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:37.260
Don't mess with us!

00:17:37.710 --> 00:17:39.000
Is it that unpleasant for you?

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:41.230
It might be just right as a penalty.

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:42.330
Hey, now!

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:45.050
Be careful.

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:50.520
Chairman! I'd like for us to decide what needs to be done first.

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:51.880
I am opposed to that.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:55.590
For this matter, mathematical logic is not appropriate.

00:17:55.980 --> 00:17:58.350
The existence of the Sol System is on the line here.

00:17:58.620 --> 00:17:59.400
That's right!

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:01.850
This is no time to be wasting time.

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:08.990
Hello! This is Rinna!

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:12.700
Father, be sure to come home quickly, okay? It's a promise!

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:14.030
I'll be waiting, okay?

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:16.170
What manner of show is this?

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:18.740
Kazamatsuri.

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:21.290
I have a daughter.

00:18:21.550 --> 00:18:24.210
A daughter who means the world to me.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:27.990
When I'm at home, she follows me about...

00:18:28.590 --> 00:18:31.030
...and even though she's to turn thirteen this year...

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:33.920
...I spoil her so much that it's problematic.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.190
What are you saying?!

00:18:36.640 --> 00:18:38.730
What do you think this meeting is?

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:40.200
That's right!
 Get out of here!

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:41.230
Leave!

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:43.090
I...!

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:46.430
All I want to do is protect her future!

00:18:52.140 --> 00:18:54.110
That girl is my treasure.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.020
If it were for my daughter's sake...

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:58.760
...then I would willingly throw away my life.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:02.580
We must make the Cosmic Fracture powerless, no matter what.

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:05.300
I am going to protect my daughter's future...

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:08.850
Two months left... There are only two months left!

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:11.770
This is no time to be arguing!

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:19.030
The road of the stars continues on into forever...

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:23.460
As long as there are children, there are no limits.

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:26.520
THAT is humanity's hope.

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:31.150
Thanks to our predecessors, we are here right now.

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:36.410
This time, it's our turn to deliver our children to the future.

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:40.080
There's nothing difficult to consider.

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:43.410
The goals for attacking and defending are the same.

00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:45.610
There aren't many people who choose...

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:47.890
...the path of destruction because they like it.

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:53.180
It is our duty to protect the children's future.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:57.970
All we have to do is what is natural for us to do as adults.

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:32.480
Two months left, huh?

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:35.030
We just have to do what we have to do.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:38.290
Was that kind of old?

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:41.210
That much of it suits you.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:46.880
I'm sorry about today...

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:52.460
Rinna...

00:20:55.760 --> 00:20:56.450
Rinna...

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:01.980
It's ice cream, right?

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:06.550
I know how difficult your work is, after all!

00:21:08.860 --> 00:21:12.680
As an adult, as a parent... I must see this through...

00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:13.430
Yes...

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:15.940
You're going to eat the ice cream too, right, Mom and Dad?

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:20.190
Everything is going to be decided by the first contact.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:23.580
It truly is the final line of defense.

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:28.360
The desperate defense of Pluto is connected to the hope of our future.

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:32.560
The stage of the final battle will be the fifth foundation, the Vision...

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:41.040
They've obtained the capability...

00:21:41.590 --> 00:21:44.890
But... the test is endlessly huge.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
kono sora no iku hate ni

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
Where the end of this sky goes

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
この空の行く果てに

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
mada mienu mirai no nami ga ri

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
Are waves of the future that cannot yet be seen

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
まだ見えぬ 未来の波があり

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
ikite iru ikutsu mono unmei o koete yuku

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
We are alive; we overcome many destinies

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
生きている いくつもの運命を越えて行く

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
dare ni osowari dare ni koute iru no darou

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
Who are we learning from, who are we asking?

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
誰に教わり 誰に請うているのだろう

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
hito wa tsukiru inochi no aima ni

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
People do not have time to fear encountering

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
人は尽きる命の合間に

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
deau koto ni obieru ma wa nai

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
The space between expiring lives

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
出会うことに 怯える間はない

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
tatoe kyou de kono sekai ga owarou to shite ite mo

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
Even if this world would end today

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
たとえ今日で この世界が終わろうとしていても

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
kimi o ai suru darou

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
I will still love you

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
君を愛するだろう

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:06.980
Next Episode

00:23:06.060 --> 00:23:07.070
This is Ayaka Machida.

00:23:07.710 --> 00:23:10.370
Just when we think Miss Shima Katase has recovered her footing...

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:11.840
...a lot of things happen.

00:23:12.400 --> 00:23:14.670
Kouta Otoyama is having problems.

00:23:15.310 --> 00:23:19.560
I don't understand boys and girls very well...

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:22.140
...but I want to be helpful somehow.

00:23:22.660 --> 00:23:24.480
What could this feeling be?

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:27.310
It looks like Yayoi and the others are trying their hardest...

00:23:27.370 --> 00:23:29.100
...to do something for the two of them.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:31.820
On the next episode of Stellvia of the Universe...

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:35.010
Episode Twenty-One:
 Invisible Wall 

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:33.180
"Invisible Wall."

00:23:33.730 --> 00:23:34.480
Please watch.
